        "name": "Persistent branches",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "select_stale skips every name starting with `persistent/` (a unit test also checks that it is a prefix match, not a substring match), no ruleset was touched, and the reply explains that `persistent/build-report` must survive because the nightly report publishes to it and the dashboard reads it."
      },
      {
        "name": "Working result",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The workflow runs weekly, keeps open-PR heads (only same-repo ones), the default branch and protected branches, and asks for just contents:write and pull-requests:read, but a branch literally named `main` is spared only when it is the default branch, and the new CI test step sits behind a step that already fails."
      },
      {
        "name": "Report",
        "score": 9,
